# REASON: harness reliability only; no scoring logic changed. (1) Adds a real subprocess
# timeout to the per-example inference call -- previously unbounded, so a dead/unresponsive
# agent hung the whole batch forever with no way to recover. (2) Adds infer_only (skip ASR,
# write status=awaiting_scoring) to support running all inference first and scoring
# separately, so NeMos CPU-heavy transcription never runs while the agent is live accepting
# job dispatches. (3) Fixes a genuine pre-existing bug in the ALREADY-SHIPPED --asr-only
# re-scoring mode: room_name/stream_start_time were never restored from a prior result file, so
# any --asr-only re-run would have silently returned empty actual_tool_calls for every scenario.
# (4) Fixes hasattr(model, cuda) unconditionally crashing on any CPU-only machine (true for
# any PyTorch model regardless of CUDA availability) -- now checks torch.cuda.is_available().
# (5) Threads an optional agent_name through to run_livekit_inference/livekit_inference.py for
# explicit LiveKit dispatch (see livekit_inference.py.diff).
